    "notes": "Segment start is the 0-based offset in the electronic-format IBAN (no spaces); values.characterClass uses the SWIFT classes n (digits), a (upper-case letters), c (upper-case letters and digits). This format is not registered with SWIFT. Treat it as a hint for display and soft validation, not as a rule. Sources disagree on the length, so no length, pattern or segments are given; see claims. Disagreements in other libraries, recorded but not followed: length: iban.js has 24, schwifty has 26; BBAN character classes: iban.js has [0-9]{20}, schwifty has [0-9]{22}; length: php-iban has 24, schwifty has 26; BBAN character classes: php-iban has [0-9]{20}, schwifty has [0-9]{22}; bankCode position in the BBAN: php-iban has none, schwifty has 0-5; branchCode position in the BBAN: php-iban has none, schwifty has 5-10; nationalCheckDigits position in the BBAN: php-iban has none, schwifty has 20-22."
